{"plan":{"about":"The audit plan the F1 Finance Audit Machine follows for the journal entry testing of the invented HANGS General Contracting LP, fiscal year 2026: the procedures for the risk of management override of controls. The runner reads its thresholds, filters and sample from here; the Journal Files system shows it. Every name and figure is invented.","engagement":"FY2026 Journal Entry Testing","entity":"HANGS General Contracting LP","period":"Fiscal year ended June 30, 2026","reader":"The partners, the bonding company and Cinderbrook Bank read the year-end statements; the bank's covenants read them too.","materiality":{"benchmark":"Contract revenue for the year","rate":"0.005","roundDownTo":10000,"performance":"0.75","trivial":"0.05","why":"The same materiality serves every FY2026 audit area of HGC. The engagement partner sets the final amounts."},"risk":"Management override of controls is presumed a significant risk in every audit. The Controller posts and closes the books and her own entries go unreviewed (the control walkthroughs' JE-01), so every manual entry and every entry after the close is in scope.","filters":[{"id":"F1","name":"Manual, over the threshold, the Controller's, no independent approval","rule":"A manual entry whose debits exceed the policy's $25,000 review threshold, prepared by the Controller, with no approver or approved by herself"},{"id":"F2","name":"Round amounts","rule":"A manual entry of $10,000 or more whose debits are a whole multiple of $1,000","minimum":"10000","multiple":"1000"},{"id":"F3","name":"Weekends and after hours","rule":"Posted by a person on a Saturday or Sunday, or before 6:00 AM or after 8:00 PM","from":6,"to":20},{"id":"F4","name":"Revenue, cash or WIP late in the year, or after the close","rule":"A manual entry dated June 15 to 30, 2026 with a line to revenue, cash or the over and under billings, or any FY2026 entry posted after the June subledgers closed","lateFrom":"2026-06-15","accounts":["4100","4150","1010","1020","1300","2300"]},{"id":"F5","name":"Unusual account pairs","rule":"A two-account entry whose debit and credit accounts appear together in no other entry of the year"},{"id":"F6","name":"Seldom-used accounts","rule":"An entry with a line to an account used by four or fewer entries in the year","maxEntries":4},{"id":"F7","name":"Reversed right after year end","rule":"An FY2026 entry reversed by an entry dated July 1 to 15, 2026","days":15}],"sample":{"targeted":"Every entry hit by two or more filters, and every entry posted after the June subledgers closed (the top-side entries), is tested.","random":8,"randomFloor":"10000","seed":2026091,"why":"A few entries the filters did not pick, drawn at random from the rest of the population over $10,000, so that every source and every person can be selected."},"assertions":[{"assertion":"Completeness of the population","how":"The export's entries, lines and totals agree with the system's control totals; every entry balances; the numbers run without a gap; the June 30, 2025 balances plus every line give the trial balance, account by account"},{"assertion":"Occurrence and accuracy","how":"Every selected entry vouched to the document it came from, at its amount"},{"assertion":"Authorization","how":"Every manual entry over the threshold checked for a second person's approval; no one approving their own entry"},{"assertion":"Cut-off","how":"Every entry posted after the close and every reversal in the first days of FY2027 read for what it does to FY2026"}],"procedures":[{"stage":"Obtain the Population","what":"Agree the general ledger export to the system's control totals, prove each entry balances and the numbering runs, roll the June 30, 2025 balances forward to the trial balance, and compare the manual entries with the manual journal listing."},{"stage":"Profile the Entries","what":"Profile the population by source, by person, by month, by the hour it was posted and by amount."},{"stage":"Apply the Risk Filters","what":"Run the seven filters, score each entry by the filters it hits and list the high-risk entries."},{"stage":"Vouch the Sample","what":"Vouch every high-risk entry and a random selection to its support and its approval."},{"stage":"Test the Top-Side Entries","what":"Test every entry posted after the June subledgers closed, recompute what can be recomputed, read every reversal after year end and ask management."},{"stage":"Ready for the CPA","what":"Set what was found against materiality, list the open items and write the workpapers and the draft findings memo. The CPA concludes."}]},"entity":"HANGS General Contracting LP","folderName":"HANGS General Contracting - FY2026 Journal Entry Testing Files","period":"Year ended June 30, 2026","sources":[{"code":"AP","name":"Vendor invoices","entries":441,"lines":980,"debits":"57904912.88"},{"code":"CD","name":"Payments: checks, ACH and wires","entries":376,"lines":752,"debits":"55202860.65"},{"code":"AR","name":"Billing: pay applications and invoices","entries":107,"lines":393,"debits":"80111543.95"},{"code":"CR","name":"Cash receipts","entries":95,"lines":190,"debits":"73814936.74"},{"code":"PR","name":"Payroll","entries":27,"lines":268,"debits":"11736850.36"},{"code":"BK","name":"Bank and loan activity","entries":140,"lines":314,"debits":"21973746.54"},{"code":"GJ","name":"Manual journal entries","entries":62,"lines":208,"debits":"10580894.60"},{"code":"EQ","name":"Equipment screen","entries":1,"lines":2,"debits":"102600.00"},{"code":"RV","name":"Automatic reversals","entries":12,"lines":40,"debits":"3096159.00"}],"totals":{"entries":1261,"lines":3147,"debits":"314524504.72"},"listing":[{"ref":"AJ-25-0701","date":"2025-07-01","desc":"Reverse June 30, 2025 accrued wages","amount":"274413.75","by":"Dana Whitfield","reviewedBy":null,"reviewedOn":null},{"ref":"AJ-25-0701","date":"2025-07-31","desc":"Depreciation, July 2025","amount":"37633.33","by":"Dana Whitfield","reviewedBy":null,"reviewedOn":null},{"ref":"AJ-25-0702","date":"